# LTX-2 Pipeline — Local-First Pivot

The objective is to get the full LTX-2 pipeline running without forced, massive downloads or gated API keys. We will leverage existing model weights already present on the user's system (Syncthing shares, LM Studio cache).

## Proposed Changes

### [Component Name] Weight Discovery & Linking
Summary: Instead of [scripts/download_weights.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it/scripts/download_weights.py) being the primary entry point, we will use a discovery script to find where the user already has these massive files and symlink them into [weights/](file:///c:/just-dub-it/server.py#79-91).

#### [NEW] [discovery.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it/scripts/discovery.py)
A script that:
1. Searches all drives (`C:`, `D:`, `I:`, `X:`, `G:`) for [ltx-2-19b-dev.safetensors](file:///c:/just-dub-it/weights/ltx-2-19b-dev.safetensors).
2. Searches for `gemma-3` model directories (HF format, not necessarily GGUF).
3. Identifies Syncthing sync folders by locating `config.xml`.
4. Offers to symlink found files into the local [weights/](file:///c:/just-dub-it/server.py#79-91) directory.

### [Component Name] Server Flexibility
#### [MODIFY] [server.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it/server.py)
Update to:
1. Check multiple possible locations for weights (e.g., direct paths or a `WEIGHTS_PATH` env var).
2. Fallback to CPU-only Gemma if necessary, or use a local path if found.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. Run `discovery.py` to find weights.
2. Confirm the [weights/](file:///c:/just-dub-it/server.py#79-91) directory contains valid links/files.
3. Boot [server.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it/server.py) and verify it reports "Weights ready: True".
